    "text": "A block of mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> moving on a horizontal surface with speed&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> enters a rough horizontal patch ranging from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>00</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. If the retarding force <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;on the block in this range is inversely proportional to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> over this range i.e.<br />\r<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi></mfrac></math>&nbsp;for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.10</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.00</mo></math><br />\r<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.10</mn><mtext> </mtext></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2.00</mn></math><br />\rIf&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math> then, the speed of this block ( in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;) as it crosses the patch is ( use&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mi>n</mi><mtext>   </mtext><mn>20</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;)"
  },
